<title>GREECE: TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</title>
<headline>TABLE OF GREEK MUTUAL FUND FLOWS, ASSETS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ionian Bank reported the</p>
<p>following daily and year-to-date changes in the volume of Greek</p>
<p>mutual fund outstanding shares, net assets and net share prices,</p>
<p>as well as total net asset sizes as of July 10.</p>
<p>				  July 10/July 09  July 10/Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>						 (%)		  (%)</p>
<p>NET SHARE PRICES*</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.03		 7.88</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.03		 6.20</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.13		12.35</p>
<p>  Growth Funds			   -0.02		54.36</p>
<p>* Prices include distributed dividends</p>
<p>VOLUME OF SHARES</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.09		37.93</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.08		38.60</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.03		15.28</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.31		32.51</p>
<p>NET ASSETS</p>
<p>  Total market			    0.12		47.02</p>
<p>  Fixed income &amp;money market funds  0.11		45.66</p>
<p>  International funds		   0.18		27.72</p>
<p>  Growth funds			    0.28		99.23</p>
<p>All calculations are based on a performance index of mutual</p>
<p>funds whose base was set to be equal to 100 on December 31,</p>
<p>1991.</p>
<p>NET ASSET SIZES (in drachmas)</p>
<p>  Total market				  5,591,181,058,326</p>
<p>  Fixed income funds			  1,987,253,006,731</p>
<p>  Money market funds			  3,259,109,583,418</p>
<p>  International funds			   100,400,317,287</p>
<p>  Growth funds				    244,418,150,890</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
